      ],
      "message": "depends: harden Linux and Windows packages\n\nThe release flags for Linux and Windows packages are only -O2. So\nsqlite, libzmq, capnp and the others are built without\n_FORTIFY_SOURCE, and on Linux without -fstack-clash-protection,\nunless the compiler turns them on by default. Debian's GCC turns on\nneither.\n\nAdd -U_FORTIFY_SOURCE -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=3 to linux_release_CFLAGS and\nmingw32_release_CFLAGS, and -fstack-clash-protection to\nlinux_release_CFLAGS. CMakeLists.txt adds the same flags to\ncore_interface. toolchain.cmake passes them to the main build as well,\nso secp256k1 also gets them in depends builds.\n\nLeave macOS alone: its SDK already fortifies, and Apple clang ignores\n-fstack-clash-protection on arm64.",
